          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Multilinear maps between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+convex+topological+vector+spaces"} locally convex topological vector spaces
            are important in many respects not least because of their use in infinite dimensional calculus as the homes of higher derivatives. However, outside the realm of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+vector+spaces"} normed vector spaces
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The definition of an
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+map"} bilinear map
          #mult.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              = succeed "-linear" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to W
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi L
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^n(V,W)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^n \to W
              with the property that they are linear in each variable.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
              we write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(V,W)
              and we extend the notation to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
              where by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^0(V,W)
              we mean just
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LCTVS"} LCTVS
            we can restrict to continuous maps.
          #cmult.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+convex+topological+vector+spaces"} locally convex topological vector spaces
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              = succeed "-linear" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to W
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n(V,W)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^n \to W
              with the property that they are linear in each variable.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
              we write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}(V,W)
              and we extend the notation to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
              where by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^0(V,W)
              we mean just
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          %p
            There are a variety of topologies that one can put on the spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n(V,W)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+sets"} bounded sets
            of the source.
          #cmtop.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LCTVS"} LCTVS
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              be a collection of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+subsets"} bounded subsets
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              which covers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_{\mathcal{S}}
              to be the topology on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n(V,W)
              given by uniform convergence on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LCTVS"} LCTVS
              structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n(V,W)
              defined by the family of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-norms"} semi-norms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi sup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho(u)_{\sigma,S} \coloneqq \sup \{\sigma(u(h_1,\dots,h_n)) : h_i \in S\}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in \mathcal{S}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi W
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \colon W \to \mathbb{R}
              is a continuous semi-norm on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %p
              We write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n_{\mathcal{S}}(V,W)
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LCTVS"} LCTVS
              with underlying vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n(V,W)
              and topology
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Λ
                        %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_{\mathcal{S}}
          %p The commonest families in use are:
          %ol
            %li
              The finite subsets. This resulting topology is known as the
              %strong simple
              topology and the usual notations are
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_s
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_s(V,W)
            %li
              The compact subsets, with notations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_k
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_k(V,W)
            %li
              The
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/precompact+subsets"} precompact subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_{p k}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_{p k}(V,W)
            %li
              The
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+subsets"} bounded subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_b
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_b(V,W)
          %p
            Of all the topologies definable using Definition
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#cmtop"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_s
            is the coarsest and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_b
            the finest.
          %p
            The topology of simple convergence (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_s
            ) also makes sense on the spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^n(V,W)
            and we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi L
                    %mi s
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_s^n(V,W)
            for the resulting LCTVS. We have that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi s
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊆
                  %msubsup
                    %mi L
                    %mi s
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_s^n(V,W) \subseteq L^n_s(V,W) \subset W^{V^n}
            (with the product topology) are topological embeddings.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                For any suitable family of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+sets"} bounded sets
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒮
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{S}}^{n+m}(V,W) \to \mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{S}}^n(V,\mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{S}}^m(V,W))
                is a topological embedding.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metrisable"} metrisable
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                arbitrary, and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
                contains all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact"} compact
                sets then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{S}}^{n+m}(V,W) \to \mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{S}}^n(V,\mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{S}}^m(V,W))
                is an isomorphism.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metrisable"} metrisable
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/barrelled"} barrelled
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                arbitrary, and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
                arbitrary then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{S}}^{n+m}(V,W) \to \mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{S}}^n(V,\mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{S}}^m(V,W))
                is an isomorphism.
          %h2#separate_continuity Separate Continuity
          %p
            The definition of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n(V,W)
            requires the maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^n \to W
            to be continuous in the product topology. On the other hand, the linearity is required only on a per-factor basis. It is possible to make the continuity requirement also work on a per-factor basis using the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                hypocontinuity
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/hypocontinuity"} ?
          #smult.num_defn
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LCTVS"} LCTVS
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              be a family of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+subsets"} bounded subsets
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              which cover
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}^n_{\mathcal{S}}(V,W)
              inductively by:
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℋ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}^0(V,W) \coloneqq W
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℋ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi 𝒮
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℋ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}^n_{\mathcal{S}}(V,W) \coloneqq \mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{S}}(V, \mathcal{H}^{n-1}_{\mathcal{S}}(V,W))
                \.
          %h2#properties_2 Properties
          %ol
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n_{\mathcal{S}}(V,W) \to \mathcal{H}^n_{\mathcal{S}}(V,W)
              is a topological embedding.
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S} \subseteq \mathcal{S}'
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mo ′
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}^n_{\mathcal{S}'}(V,W)
              injects continuously into
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℋ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}^n_{\mathcal{S}}(V,W)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mi s
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}^n_s(V,W)
              consists of the
              %span.newWikiWord
                separately continuous
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/separately+continuous"} ?
              multilinear maps
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^n \to W
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metrisable"} metrisable
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              contains all compact sets, or if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metrisable"} metrisable
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/barrelled"} barrelled
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℋ
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n_{\mathcal{S}}(V,W) = \mathcal{H}^n_{\mathcal{S}}(V,W)
          %h2#convergence_structures Convergence Structures
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
            defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+vector+space"} convergence vector space
            with the same underlying vector space and the same continuous mappings (that is to say, the functor from topological vector spaces to convergence vector spaces is full and faithful and respects the vector space functor). The construction of the spaces of continuous multilinear operators makes sense for convergence vector spaces as well as for topological ones. The resulting spaces of multilinear operators has several useful structures as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+vector+space"} convergence vector space
            which are not topological.
          #cvs.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              be
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+vector+spaces"} convergence vector spaces
              %strong continuous convergence
              structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n(V,W)
              is the coarsest convergence structure which makes the evaluation map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n(V,W) \times V^n \to W
              continuous. The resulting convergence space (which is a convergence vector space) is written
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi c
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n_c(V,W)
            %p
              The structure of
              %strong bounded convergence
              (resp.
              = succeed ")" do
                %strong quasi-bounded convergence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n(V,W)
              is defined by the following requirement: for every filter
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^n(V,W)
              and every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \in \mathcal{L}^n(V,W)
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo →
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} \to u
              if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo −
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{F} - u)(\mathcal{B}^n) \to 0
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              for every bounded (resp. quasi-bounded) filter
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi b
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_b^n(V,W)
              (resp.
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mrow
                          %mi q
                          %mi b
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_{q b}^n(V,W)
          %p
            Recall that a filter is
            %em bounded
            if it contains a bounded set and is
            %em quasi-bounded
            if the filter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒱
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V} \cdot \mathcal{F} \to 0
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒱
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            is the filter of
            = succeed "-neighbourhoods" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
          %p
            If both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            are LCTVS then the two notions of bounded convergence agree.
